<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#aerial-bombardment">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aerial bombardment</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aerial bombardment is the use of aircraft to drop bombs or other munitions on military or civilian targets. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> was among the first states to use it in war, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> in 1911, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a> employed it extensively in the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> in 1935–1936, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chemical-weapons">chemical weapons</a>. Its use against forces with little air defence contributed to the defeat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aerial-bombardment.jpg" alt="Aerial bombardment" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: US Air Force · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bombardement_du_Grand_B%C3%A9_par_des_B-24_Liberators_de_la_8th_Air_Force_am%C3%A9ricaine_en_ao%C3%BBt_1944..jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Italy's 1935 invasion, which used <b>aerial bombardment</b> and poison gas to capture Addis Ababa in May 1936, was the gravest external threat since Ahmad Gran, but Haile Selassie returned in triumph on 5 May 1941 following British-assisted liberation.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The Second Italo-Ethiopian War of 1935–1936, led by Emilio De Bono and then Pietro Badoglio, ended in the conquest of Ethiopia through numerical superiority, mechanised forces, <b>aerial bombardment</b> and the use of chemical weapons.</blockquote><a href="/empire/italian-empire">Italian Empire · Military</a></li></ul></section>
